    "probe_text": "Here is the full ordered account, read straight from `owners.POST.yml` and its function classes. I'll mark each item as **[V]** validation (can reject the request) or **[S]** side-effect (mutation / persistence / logging).\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **[V] Authorization** \u2014 the whole file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`).\n\n## Step 1 \u2014 `CheckIdempotencyKey` (no governance; in-memory only)\n- **[S]** Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` request header and **publishes** it as an `IdempotencyKey` variable for later steps.\n- **[V]/branch** If the key was seen before (present in the in-memory `IdempotencyStore`), it **short-circuits to the replay branch**: `LoadOwnerById` \u2192 `RespondWithOwner` under a *readonly* transaction, returning the originally created owner with **200** and running none of the create logic below. Otherwise it proceeds to the fresh-create pipeline.\n\n*(Everything below is the fresh-create path.)*\n\n## Step 2 \u2014 `ValidateOwnerFields` (`@RequestBody`; the one body binding)\nRuns in this internal order:\n- **[S] Address normalization** (`OwnerAddress.applyStructured`) \u2014 normalizes `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` (trim, collapse internal whitespace, uppercase, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`), writes them back, and composes the effective flat `address` (structured fields preferred over the flat form). Done first so the blank check sees the normalized value.\n- **[V] Required fields** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must each be non-null and non-blank. All offenders are collected and reported together as **400** (`MissingOwnerFieldsException`).\n- **[S]/[V] Telephone \u2192 E.164** (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`) \u2014 strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+`+country code, else assumes `+61` and drops one leading `0`; requires 8\u201315 digits, and for recognized codes an exact national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u21d2 **400** (`InvalidTelephoneException`). The normalized value is **stored back** on the request.\n- **[S]/[V] Email** (`OwnerEmail.normalize`) \u2014 optional; if present, trim, regex-validate, lowercase, and reject disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). Invalid/disposable \u21d2 **400** (`InvalidEmailException`). Normalized value **stored back**; absent email left untouched.\n- **[V] Postcode** (`OwnerPostcode.validate`) \u2014 optional; if present must be exactly 4 digits, and for a city with a known region within that range (`NSW 2000\u20132099`, `VIC 3000\u20133099`, `QLD 4000\u20134099`; unknown region \u21d2 any 4-digit ok). Invalid \u21d2 **400** (`InvalidPostcodeException`). Value is **not** modified.\n- **[S]** Publishes the validated `OwnerFieldsDto` as a variable for later steps.\n\n## Step 3 \u2014 `ResolveRegistrationDate`\n- **[V] Future date** \u2014 a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server's current date \u21d2 **400** (`FutureRegistrationDateException`).\n- **[S]** Computes the effective date (supplied, else today), rolls it forward off weekends and listed public holidays (`BusinessDay.adjust`), and **publishes** the adjusted `LocalDate`. Every later date-derived value uses this.\n\n## Step 4 \u2014 `CheckCityCapacity` (transaction)\n- **[V]** Counts existing owners in the same city (case-insensitive). At **\u2265 50** \u21d2 **409** (`CityAtCapacityException`).\n\n## Step 5 \u2014 `CheckDailyOwnerLimit` (transaction)\n- **[V]** Counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the adjusted date. At **\u2265 DAILY_LIMIT** \u21d2 **429** (`DailyOwnerLimitException`).\n\n## Step 6 \u2014 `BuildOwner` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Maps the request to an `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper`) and sets its `registrationDate` to the adjusted date. Publishes the `Owner` (not yet persisted).\n\n## Step 7 \u2014 `AssignHousehold` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `householdId` = first 12 hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + \"|\" + postcode` (assigned to every owner).\n\n## Step 8 \u2014 `CheckUniqueIdentity` (transaction)\n- **[V]** If `sharesHousehold=true`, bypass. Otherwise, if the new owner's `householdId` matches any existing **non-deleted** owner \u21d2 **409** (`DuplicateIdentityException`).\n\n## Step 9 \u2014 `CheckPossibleDuplicate` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. `sharesHousehold=true` \u21d2 both cleared (`false`/null). Otherwise flags `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf`=earliest matching id when an existing non-deleted owner shares `lastName`+`postcode` but has a **different** telephone. (This is a flag, not a rejection.)\n\n## Step 10 \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode/city; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`), appending `-n` (n\u22652) to de-collide with existing customer codes.\n\n## Step 11 \u2014 `AssignMembershipNumber` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `membershipNumber` = `customerCode + \"-M\" + YY`, where YY is the two-digit fiscal year (starting 1 July) of the adjusted `registrationDate`.\n\n## Step 12 \u2014 `CountNamesakes` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing the same first+last name (case-insensitive), counted before save (excludes self).\n\n## Step 13 \u2014 `FlagBulkSignup` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Sets `bulkSignupWarning` = `true` when existing owners on the same `registrationDate` exceed **80** (`BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD`), else `false`.\n\n## Step 14 \u2014 `SaveOwner` (transaction)\n- **[S]** `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 persists the owner and assigns its generated id. This is the core write.\n\n## Step 15 \u2014 `RecordIdempotencyKey` (transaction)\n- **[S]** If the request carried an `Idempotency-Key`, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory `IdempotencyStore` (so a later repeat replays this owner). No-op when no key.\n\n## Step 16 \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (transaction)\n- **[S]** Stamps `householdMemberCount` (`HouseholdMembers.stamp`, counting stored owners including the just-saved one), maps to `OwnerDto`, writes an **AUDIT log line** (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber), and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\n## Transaction boundary\nSteps 4\u201316 all carry `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the writes (save + idempotency record) commit **once** at the end of the pipeline; any escalation thrown earlier prevents persistence.\n\nOne note worth surfacing: the body is bound with plain `@RequestBody` (no `@Valid`) in `ValidateOwnerFields`, so JSR-303 bean validation on `OwnerFieldsDto` does **not** run here \u2014 all field validation is the explicit logic above (the `MethodArgumentNotValidException` escalation handler that exists in the project is not exercised by this endpoint)."
